2012-06-07 18:54 – Byron Arnold:
> I have been playing Nethack on and off for a couple years. I'll usually go through a phase of obsession, followed by a much longer phase of being burnt out on it after not getting any noticeably better.
I guess we all did so.  It was the same for me, at least.

> Yesterday, I finally reached the Oracle. Farthest I have ever made it. Of course, I bypassed the Gnomish Mines (I had read that the game is easier if you put off the mines until after Sokoban. Can anyone confirm/repusiate this for me?). It was no fun once I got there, though. While dipping my long sword in the fountains (I was a level 5 lawful knight), I called up a nymph who stole my (very rusty) sword. Then there was another nymph, and a leprechaun. Betwee the three of them, they left me broke and defenseless. (The nymphs would steal even more from me when I would chase them down to get my stuff back) I ever made it past the Oracle...
Congratulations!

Some things in the mines are worth the trouble, IMHO.  I usually go down
until Minetown before doing Sokoban.  This gives me a pick-axe, decent
enough armor, a good stack of daggers for throwing around, a guaranteed
altar and some shops for doing price-identification.  Sometimes even a
magic lamp…  Deeper than that, I wouldn't venture until at least past
Sokoban.

Even with a weak role like tourist, I like to stay in the first mines
level (usually close to the upstairs) until I got the good stuff off at
least one dwarf: a pick-axe, a dwarfish mithril coat, iron shoes, a
dwarfish iron helm, a dwarfish cloak, and possibly a dwarfish
roundshield.  This puts me to at least AC 0 if none of it is cursed,
which greatly improves my chances of making it to the Oracle…  ;-)

> Anyways, proud of my new milestone! Hopefully, I can get past the Mines, Oracle, and Sokoban soon! :)
Hope you do so!  After the Oracle, I'd try to reach Sokoban ASAP.  It's
the spare upstairs in the level immediately below the Oracle.  Sokoban
is relatively easy, gives you food enough for the rest of the game, and
can also provide some good rings and wands (and the main prize, of
course).  After that, an identifying session to separate junk from
escape items can further improve your fare.

